brief:
Write the pull request description for this firmware change so reviewers understand why it exists. Ticket FW-482. Problem: three units in a Lisbon warehouse raised false 100% humidity alarms when a glitched read returned 0xFFFF, and field battery life is only about 14 months because of 500 ms sampling (average 212 µA). Bench results with the change: average current 96 µA, noise down from ±1.8 %RH to ±0.6 %RH. Four reads take about 150 ms, so we feed the watchdog (1 s timeout) inside the loop. Risk: alarms can now be detected up to 2 s late instead of 0.5 s; product says the limit is 5 s. Not tested below -10 C.

--- a/src/sensor/humidity.c
+++ b/src/sensor/humidity.c
@@ -41,14 +41,22 @@
-#define SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS 500
+#define SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS 2000
+#define SAMPLES_PER_AVG  4

 int humidity_read(float *out)
 {
-    uint16_t raw = read_raw();
-    *out = raw * 100.0f / 65535.0f;
-    return 0;
+    uint32_t sum = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < SAMPLES_PER_AVG; i++) {
+        uint16_t raw = read_raw();
+        if (raw == 0xFFFF) {
+            return -EIO;
+        }
+        sum += raw;
+        wdt_feed();
+    }
+    *out = (sum / SAMPLES_PER_AVG) * 100.0f / 65535.0f;
+    return 0;
 }
